  "assumptions": [
    "The system serves a single store (single location), so stock is tracked once per product in inventory_levels; multi-location support would require a stores/locations table and a location_id on inventory_levels and stock_movements.",
    "Each user has exactly one role (many-to-one users to roles); roles map to granular permissions through the role_permissions junction table, and RBAC is enforced in the API layer.",
    "Roles are seeded with Store Owner, Store Manager and Store Clerk; permissions are seeded per API endpoint/function.",
    "Every table has exactly one primary key column; junction tables (role_permissions, product_suppliers, purchase_order_items) use a surrogate uuid id plus a composite unique index on their foreign key pair.",
    "Primary keys are uuid generated by gen_random_uuid() except high-volume append-only tables (stock_movements, login_attempts), which use bigint identity keys.",
    "Stock movements are append-only; corrections are made by new movements, never by editing history. inventory_levels.quantity_on_hand is updated in the same transaction as the stock_movements insert and uses the version column for optimistic concurrency.",
    "Sales are recorded as stock_movements of type sale (with unit_price snapshot) because a full point-of-sale order model is outside the stated requirements; top sellers and turnover are derived from this ledger.",
    "Stock value is computed as quantity_on_hand multiplied by products.unit_cost; low-stock counts are computed from inventory_levels versus products.reorder_threshold.",
    "Unknown barcodes are not stored; the application offers to create a new product and product_barcodes row when a scan finds no match.",
    "Passwords are stored only as bcrypt hashes in users.password_hash; deactivated users keep their row (is_active=false) so history remains intact, and failed login attempts are logged in login_attempts.",
    "Real-time propagation to clients is handled by the application over WebSockets; the database only needs fast indexed reads and writes (barcode and product_id indexes).",
    "Monetary values use decimal and quantities use int; timestamps are stored in UTC.",
    "Enumerated fields (status, movement_type, report_type) are stored as varchar and validated by application logic or CHECK constraints."
  ]
}